<title>POLAND: Russian PM says IMF may resume loans from Dec 15.</title>
<headline>Russian PM says IMF may resume loans from Dec 15.</headline>
<dateline>ZEBOWO, Poland 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Prime Minister Viktor Chernomyrdin said on Thursday that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) was likely to resume its loan payments to Russia from December 15.</p>
<p>&quot;We have completed discussions with Mr. (IMF President Michel) Camdessus, we've gone through all aspects of the agreement between Russia and IMF and I think that from December 15 the payments will be resumed,&quot; Chernomyrdin told a news conference during his visit to Poland.</p>
</text>
